Day 20: Gen AI for Beginners

Generative AI is a type of AI that creates new content such as text, music, video, and images by learning patterns from existing data, mimicking human creative work.

There are multiple models in ML like:
Prediction models like regression
Classification problems
Recommendation problems

ML was never much used in creative platforms. Gen AI changed that.
That creative power is a big strength of Gen AI.
People used to say AI cannot replace human creativity.

Path: AI -> ML -> DL -> Gen AI
AI has many techniques. ML is the main one.
ML has many techniques. DL is used a lot.
DL has many techniques. Gen AI is popular now.

Why Gen AI became so important in about three years. Impact areas:
1. Customer support: chatbots try to solve the problem first. Only when the chatbot fails does a human support person step in.
2. Content creation: blogs, video, and more. This is a main place Gen AI has reached.
3. Education: a personal tutor available all the time.
4. Software development: Gen AI writes code and makes programming easier.

Is Gen AI successful?
Yes. Gen AI is successful.

Compare to other big tech stories: the internet, and crypto and blockchain.
Important questions:
Will it solve real world problems? The internet fixed real world problems. Crypto did not solve many daily real world problems. Gen AI is solving real world problems.
Is it useful day by day? Yes.
Is it impacting the world economy? Yes.
Is it creating new jobs? Yes. New roles like AI engineer, AI automation, and AI integration.
Is it accessible? Yes. Gen AI is accessible.

Why not Gen AI? (why people hesitate)
This tech feels new.
It might be a bubble.
Gen AI always brings a new term, a new tool, a new paper. It feels overwhelming.

Problems of Gen AI:
Very fast progress.
A lot of noise: FOMO merchants make people feel demotivated.
No single source to learn.

Solution: mental models.

Main important idea: foundation models.
A foundation model is an AI model trained on very large data.
Task specific models only do one kind of job.
Foundation models are generalized. They have many parameters and much data.
Best example of a foundation model: LLM (large language model).
An LLM can do many things.
Foundation models do not only predict next content. They can do multiple tasks.
Not only LLMs. There are also multimodal models (sometimes called LMMs): text, sound, image, and more.

Gen AI has two paths:
Make an LLM / foundation model
Or use an LLM / foundation model

User perspective or builder perspective.
Any new term you hear is usually one or the other.

Examples:
Prompt engineering: user perspective
RLHF (to help safeguard the LLM): builder perspective
RAG: user perspective
Pre training: builder perspective
Quantization (optimize the LLM to run in more environments): builder perspective
AI agent: user perspective
Vector DB: user perspective
Fine tuning: both user and builder

Builder curriculum:
Prerequisite: PyTorch or TensorFlow.
Step 1: Transformer architecture (how self attention works, and more)
Step 2: Types of transformers: encoder only like BERT, decoder only like GPT
Step 3: Pre training: training objectives, tokenization strategies, training strategies, handling challenges, evaluation
Step 4: Optimization: training optimization, model compression, inference optimization
Step 5: Fine tuning: task specific tuning, instruction tuning, continual pre training
Step 6: Evaluation
Step 7: Deployment

User perspective path:
Step 1: Build basic LLM apps: open source, closed source, LLM APIs, LangChain, Hugging Face, Llama, frameworks like LangChain
Step 2: Improve the LLM
  1. Prompt engineering: get better responses
  2. RAG: give personal data to the LLM
  3. Fine tuning at the user level
Step 3: AI agents: the LLM does work for you, like booking a ticket
Step 4: LLM Ops: deploy the application (many libraries exist)
Step 5: Miscellaneous: e.g. Stable Diffusion and more

Do we need to learn both?
Data scientist: more builder level
Software developer: more user side
Combination: AI engineer
An AI engineer knows foundation model ideas from the builder side and can work on both sides.
